+For named queries, the <a href="search.html#standard">standard search parameters</a> described for
+<a href="search.html#advanced">named queries</a> are potentially available for use. This includes
+search parameters for all resources and search result parameters; when a query operation is defined
+in the context of one or more resource types, search parameters for those resource types are also
+potentially available. "In scope" means the parameters are defined for use; it does not mean that
+every server supports them. Servers only need to support such inherited parameters when explicitly
+documented, and clients should not assume support for parameters that are not also advertised for
+general searches in the server's <a href="capabilitystatement.html">CapabilityStatement</a>. To
+ensure consistent behavior, authors should include relevant search parameters in the named query
+OperationDefinition or a server-specific constrained OperationDefinition.
